<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Chocolatey package for Keylo. Installs the NSIS setup from the GitHub release (see tools/). -->
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2015/06/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>keylo</id>
    <version>1.7.18</version>
    <title>Keylo</title>
    <authors>tulde23</authors>
    <owners>tulde23</owners>
    <projectUrl>https://github.com/tulde23/keylo</projectUrl>
    <projectSourceUrl>https://github.com/tulde23/keylo</projectSourceUrl>
    <packageSourceUrl>https://github.com/tulde23/keylo/tree/main/packaging/chocolatey</packageSourceUrl>
    <docsUrl>https://github.com/tulde23/keylo#readme</docsUrl>
    <bugTrackerUrl>https://github.com/tulde23/keylo/issues</bugTrackerUrl>
    <iconUrl>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tulde23/keylo/main/app/src-tauri/icons/128x128.png</iconUrl>
    <licenseUrl>https://github.com/tulde23/keylo/blob/main/LICENSE</licenseUrl>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/tulde23/keylo/releases/tag/v1.7.18</releaseNotes>
    <tags>secrets secrets-manager password-manager mcp ai-agents claude-code credentials windows-hello cli foss</tags>
    <summary>Secrets manager that lets AI agents use your API keys and tokens without seeing them.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[Keylo keeps your API keys, passwords and tokens on your PC, protected by your Windows account, and hands them to the commands that need them, never to the AI agent that runs those commands.

- **Agents use secrets without seeing them:** its MCP server and `keylo run` start commands with secrets as environment variables, and values in the output are replaced with `[keylo:name]`.
- **Access keys and approvals:** each agent gets a key covering chosen secrets; anything else needs your approval with Windows Hello.
- **Audit log** of every use, a desktop app, linked 1Password and AWS Secrets Manager items, end-to-end encrypted sync, and import from and export to other password managers.

No server and no account. The installer is per user (`%LOCALAPPDATA%\Keylo`) and adds `keylo` to your PATH.
]]></description>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
